JARVIS
Production-Grade Windows AI Voice Assistant
Complete Pin-to-Pin Build Specification
You are not being asked to create a simple chatbot.
You are being asked to engineer a complete Windows desktop AI assistant called JARVIS.
JARVIS should behave like a practical computer-control assistant inspired by the concept of Tony Stark's
JARVIS and modern voice operating systems.
The user should be able to control their Windows computer naturally using their voice.
The fundamental experience is:
CTRL + ALT → JARVIS wakes → JARVIS listens → JARVIS understands → JARVIS determines what the user
means → JARVIS uses the correct computer capability → JARVIS performs the action → JARVIS verifies
the result → JARVIS speaks back → JARVIS returns to idle
The user should NOT have to manually open a chatbot window every time.
JARVIS should run quietly in the Windows background and be available system-wide.
